### 5.3. Recommendations for Future Work
To transition this proof-of-concept simulation into an active municipal planning utility, future work should prioritize replacing flat-earth routing approximations with network-constrained models directly over Vienna's topological road graph. Integrating real-time transit schedules and weather feeds will provide critical context to improve saturation forecasting. Additionally, migrating from GBTs to distributed deep learning sequence models (e.g., LSTMs or TCNs) inside Spark would enhance capacity to capture complex non-linear correlations. Finally, deploying the Structured Streaming pipeline onto a production Kubernetes cluster will allow for empirical validation of latency and horizontal scalability under live loads.

